      "writtenOn": "2023-03-25T03:26:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Pierre,\n\nCan we have a secure way for `pvmfw` and/or VM to know whether the device is locked or not? On host, we read sysprop but not sure whether `pvmfw` can read the .\n\nOn Pixels, we wipe DPM when we lock device, but we might not expect the same thing for other devices.\n\nsee: b/238261271 for previous discussion.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 243,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "292c885184d85818d0607d1de03d1320406c859e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1eab5a9_1436387c",
        "filename": "pvmfw/README.md",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 245,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T05:21:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pvmfw _has_ to trust ABL but as an extra check we could require ABL to set one of the configuration data flag bits to reflect whether the device is locked or not. Nothing would prevent a faulty ABL from forgetting to set the flag and passing the DTBO but I guess the same could be said about the host\u0027s flag, right? WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "5072a58e_fd5d7e9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 243,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "292c885184d85818d0607d1de03d1320406c859e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0694d94_10af2285",
        "filename": "pvmfw/README.md",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 245,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T06:57:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you\u0027re proposing AVF debug policy nodes to include extra DT properties to tell host\u0027s locked stated. Am I correct? My gut feeling is that it only increases the manufacturer\u0027s burden when passing debug policies and doesn\u0027t increase security. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "f1eab5a9_1436387c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 243,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "292c885184d85818d0607d1de03d1320406c859e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
